 "_doc": "King Arthur (GAME_DESIGN.md: Heroes; art 10/31/2026). Built by tools/art/build_king_arthur.py on the shared body in tools/art/hero_kit.py; rules in docs/ART_RULES.md. From Malory, Le Morte d'Arthur (book 1 ch. 25: Excalibur and its scabbard, worn here at his side) and Geoffrey of Monmouth (Historia Regum Britanniae 9.4: armed in a coat of mail), with the crown and short beard of the medieval Nine Worthies pictures. A gold crown, a coat of mail under a blue surcoat with a gold crown on the chest (the three crowns on blue given to Arthur in medieval rolls of arms, shown as one at this size), mail on arms and legs, leather boots. Fair skin of Britain. Excalibur is drawn separately (data/art/weapons/) at his hand.",
